---
import PageLayout from "../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const faqs = [
  { q: "Does Mistral let me export my Le Chat history?", a: "Yes, Mistral offers a data export tool at admin.mistral.ai/account/export. TotalRecalls converts this raw JSON into a perfectly formatted, UTF-8 preserved Markdown library that you can actually browse." },
  { q: "Will accented and non-English text survive?", a: "Yes. TotalRecalls preserves UTF-8 throughout, so multilingual conversations stay readable." },
  { q: "Does it work on the free tier as well as Le Chat Pro?", a: "Yes. Both share the same web UI, so both download through the same path." },
];

// The visible FAQ and the FAQPage schema are generated from the SAME array, so they cannot
// drift apart. Answers are plain text on purpose: JSON-LD must match what the reader sees.
const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
const faqHtml = faqs.map((f) => `<dt>${esc(f.q)}</dt><dd>${esc(f.a)}</dd>`).join("");

const faqLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
  })),
};
---
<PageLayout title="Mistral vs. TotalRecalls" description="Mistral (Le Chat) has no built-in export. TotalRecalls reads your local session and saves every conversation as UTF-8 Markdown + JSON, so French, German and Spanish text stay intact." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Compare", href: "/compare/" }, { label: "Mistral" }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />

  <h1>Mistral vs. TotalRecalls</h1>
  <p>Mistral is the dominant non-US chat product in the EU. If your work happens in Le Chat, that history is worth keeping in a place you control.</p>

  <h2>What &ldquo;download&rdquo; usually means</h2>
  <p>Mistral provides a data export tool at admin.mistral.ai/account/export that generates a JSON archive of your Le Chat history. TotalRecalls converts this raw JSON into a perfectly formatted, UTF-8 preserved Markdown library that you can actually browse.</p>

  <h2>Why Mistral specifically</h2>
  <p>Most consumer chat products are US-based. Mistral is the most common alternative for people who want their work in European jurisdictions &mdash; and backing up locally complements that. Even if your provider is European, your archive living on your own disk is a different guarantee than a vendor holding it.</p>
  <p>TotalRecalls preserves <strong>UTF-8 throughout</strong>, so French, German, Spanish, Italian and Portuguese conversations stay readable in any editor. That makes it a genuine fit for multilingual research and translation work, not just an English-language tool.</p>

  <h2>What TotalRecalls does</h2>
  <p>TotalRecalls runs on your PC, connects to your Mistral Le Chat session locally, and writes conversations into folders as Markdown + JSON.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>Mistral Official Export</th><th>TotalRecalls</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Official export available</td><td>Yes (JSON dump)</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Multilingual text</td><td>Often mangled</td><td>UTF-8 preserved</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Formatting</td><td>Flattened</td><td>Markdown + JSON</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Scales past a handful of chats</td><td>No</td><td>Full history</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sits with your other AI tools</td><td>No</td><td>Same library, all 8 providers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p><strong>About the Pro tier:</strong> Mistral&rsquo;s Le Chat Pro tier does not expose conversation history through the public API. TotalRecalls reads from your browser session, which works for the free tier and any tier that shares the same web UI. Run the download while your session is still active &mdash; Mistral sessions expire on inactivity.</p>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <dl class="faq" set:html={faqHtml} />

  <p><em>Next:</em> <a href="/guides/mistral/">step-by-step Mistral guide</a> &middot; <a href="/download/">Download for Windows</a> &middot; <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></p>
</PageLayout>
